From 5643b12d8e3b44a04f63c5d01843d4f8713f78fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yulun Zeng <yulunz@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:31:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/32] [DevTools] Restrict renderer request overrides from
 untrusted clients

Blink's InspectorNetworkAgent applies Network.setExtraHTTPHeaders
overrides (extra headers and a Referer override) to every subresource
request. Untrusted clients such as chrome.debugger extensions may not be
allowed to access every origin (e.g. the Chrome Web Store), but the
renderer cannot evaluate the browser's attach policy, so such a client
could inject headers or a spoofed Referer into credentialed requests to
restricted origins.

For requests from untrusted clients:
- never override the Referer or apply other fetch-forbidden headers,
  which are not covered by CORS preflights;
- skip extra headers on cross-origin no-cors requests, which have no
  preflight that would let the target origin reject them;
- record the extra headers added to no-cors requests, and strip them in
  ResourceLoader when the request redirects to another origin.

Trusted clients are unaffected.

Bug: 553259600
